30,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a real problem with accountability during outages and a tendency for our initial plans to become obsolete almost immediately. We need a vendor with clear ownership.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The reality on the ground is harsh. Our peak season allows no downtime, and our hardware is a mess of old models that don't play well with generic tools.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"I've found that we struggle with maintaining our own on-site systems and that outsourcing data migration has left us with lingering errors. We can't afford more ""repair work.""","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing our internal experts, and new hires are hard to find. Furthermore, trainers' standard methods are being ignored by supervisors in favor of old habits.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Fascinating. It appears the board is allergic to capital expenditure but quite happy to let operating costs bleed us dry, especially with fragmented, separately licensed add-ons.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that sounds like a nightmare for budgeting. @Ryuji, if the hardware is that old, does that mean we need a vendor who can provide on-site engineering?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. A generic cloud suite might look good in a demo, but if it can't handle our specific yard devices or a zero-freeze window, it's useless.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, if the supervisors are ignoring trainers, then a partner firm handling training—like some vendors do—might just be a waste of money.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree, May. We need someone who stays through the rollout to ensure the system actually fits the way the crews work, not just a one-time training session.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. If we opt for a modular system with separate licenses, we are essentially inviting those creeping operating costs I discovered in the invoices.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Midori,,"So we need a vendor that offers a unified support structure to avoid the ""finger-pointing"" I saw, and a flexible configuration that doesn't break when the business changes.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm leaning toward something that isn't just a ""hosted suite."" We need something that survives the depot floor and the peak-season chaos.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm wary of anything that requires us to manage the upgrades ourselves on our own racks, given our history of skipping them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I'm worried about the transition. With our administrators retiring, we can't handle a complex migration or a system that requires high internal technical maintenance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are looking for a balance: avoiding the ""death by a thousand cuts"" of separate licenses, while ensuring the system doesn't collapse under the weight of our actual operations.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we all want stability and clear accountability. I'll be looking for a vendor that provides a cohesive package rather than a fragmented one.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will prioritize the one that can actually survive our hardware and our calendar.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,May,,I'll vote against anything that looks like it will just age in place or leave us cleaning up a botched data migration.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I'll support the option that provides the most hands-on help for our stretched staff and stubborn supervisors.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall cast my vote for the option that offers the most predictable cost structure, preferably avoiding the trap of escalating subscription add-ons.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
