55,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate A offers a hosted suite and a regional service team, which addresses my concern about fragmented support and ownership.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate D is built for transport operators and has an engineering team present through rollout. That's the only way to handle our yard devices and peak season.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate D puts it on our own servers, which I fear will lead to the same skipped upgrades we had with the dispatch tool. Candidate A is hosted.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D's engineering team being present through rollout is huge for our supervisors and retiring admins. Candidate B's partner firm isn't enough.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate C is a modular disaster waiting to happen with those separate licenses. Candidate A's fixed configuration is safer for the budget than B's marketplace.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, @Misaki, I see the appeal of D, but if the configuration is too rigid or the servers fail, we're back to the outage problem. A's regional team is a good middle ground.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the risk of skipped upgrades is real, but a ""fixed configuration"" like A's will likely fail the moment our warehouse rules change again. D is built for us.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, ""built for us"" often means ""hard to update."" I prefer the hosted nature of A or B to ensure we aren't stuck in 2012 again.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the ""hosted"" part doesn't help the depot supervisors who are currently ignoring the trainers. We need the engineering team from D on-site.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B's ""application marketplace"" is a euphemism for ""more monthly bills."" I cannot support B. Between A and D, A is more fiscally predictable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Midori,,"If we go with A, we get a hosted suite and a service team. It's a balance. But D's on-site presence is very tempting for the rollout.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A's ""fixed configuration"" is a red flag. Our business changes too fast. D is the only one that understands the transport industry's specific pressures.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"I still can't get past the ""own servers"" part of D. We've proven we can't maintain them. A is the most professional, stable choice.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I have to prioritize the people. Our admins are leaving. We need the engineering team from D to bridge that gap, or the system will fail regardless of where it's hosted.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I appreciate the technical needs, the financial risk of D's on-site deployment and potential maintenance costs is higher than A's hosted model.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'll weigh the support team of A against the rollout support of D. I think the regional service team in A is sufficient for long-term harmony.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm sticking with D. It's the only one that won't be ""ringed with spreadsheets"" within a month.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for A. It avoids the pitfalls of our past: no on-site server neglect and no fragmented licensing.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for D. The human cost of a failed rollout is too high to ignore.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will vote for A. It is the most rational choice for the budget and avoids the modular pricing trap of C and the marketplace of B.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
